  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef batch_norm_forward(x: list, gamma: list, beta: list, eps: float = 1e-5) -> np.ndarray:\n    arr = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    g = np.asarray(gamma, dtype=float)\n    b = np.asarray(beta, dtype=float)\n    if arr.ndim == 2:\n        mean = arr.mean(axis=0)\n        var = arr.var(axis=0)\n        x_hat = (arr - mean) / np.sqrt(var + eps)\n        out = g * x_hat + b\n    elif arr.ndim == 4:\n        mean = arr.mean(axis=(0, 2, 3), keepdims=True)\n        var = arr.var(axis=(0, 2, 3), keepdims=True)\n        x_hat = (arr - mean) / np.sqrt(var + eps)\n        out = g.reshape(1, -1, 1, 1) * x_hat + b.reshape(1, -1, 1, 1)\n    else:\n        mean = arr.mean(axis=0)\n        var = arr.var(axis=0)\n        out = g * ((arr - mean) / np.sqrt(var + eps)) + b\n    return np.round(out, 6)\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
